<title>IRAN: Barbie doll lives on in Iran.</title>
<headline>Barbie doll lives on in Iran.</headline>
<dateline>TEHRAN 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Reports of the demise of U.S. Mattel Inc's Barbie doll in the Islamic republic of Iran may have been exaggerated.</p>
<p>Four versions of the blonde icon in various sporty outfits -- including Friendship Barbie -- were prominently displayed in one central Tehran toy shop window on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Iran's religious rulers last year declared Barbie un-Islamic and ordered the sale of the imported doll to be stopped.</p>
<p>Other toys in the shop window included miniature models of U.S. navy and air force planes and a NASA space rocket, a Superman figure and Father Christmas in a jalopy.</p>
